      "worked": "At the minimum $A$, the tangent has gradient $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=e^x-2\\\\e^x-2&=0\\\\e^x&=2\\\\x&=\\ln2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into the function:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=e^{\\ln2}-2\\ln2\\\\y&=2-2\\ln2\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $A=(\\ln2,\\,2-2\\ln2)$.",
